{{Quote|The refugee Mon Cala city-ships in the Telaris cometary cloud have completed their conversion into war production facilities. The ''Profundity'' will be among the first combat-ready cruisers. Will supply ongoing updates as the launch date grows closer.|Anj Zavor, in a message to Mon Mothma|<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>}}
[[Colonel]] '''Anj Zavor''' was a [[human]] who served in [[Rebel Fleet Command|Fleet Command]] for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]]. He provided a report to [[Commander-in-Chief|Commander]] [[Mon Mothma]] on the militarization of [[Mon Calamari]] [[city-ship]]s in the [[Telaris cometary cloud]] and the [[Mission to Ryloth (Phoenix Squadron)|capture]] of a [[Quasar Fire-class cruiser-carrier|''Quasar Fire''-class cruiser-carrier]] that had occurred in [[3 BBY]]. Zavor then became liaison between [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]], head of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]], and the [[Massassi Group|rebels]] based in the [[Great Temple]] on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]].

In [[1 BBY]], he attended a meeting in the temple where [[Alliance High Command]] discussed the possibility of stealing the [[Death Star plans|plans]] to the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]] but ultimately decided against it. After a [[Rogue One|rogue squad]] of rebels set out to [[Battle of Scarif|steal]] the plans anyway, Raddus [[Commanding officer|led]] a [[fleet]] to support them. Zavor then kept a line of communication open between Yavin 4 and Raddus during the ensuing Battle of [[Scarif]]. Raddus [[Death|perished]] during the battle, but the successful acquisition of the plans allowed the Alliance to destroy the [[Death Star]] at the [[Battle of Yavin]], after which Zavor attended an [[Royal Award Ceremony|award ceremony]] for the victors.

==Biography==
===Liaison to Raddus===
{{Quote|We've acquired a ''Quasar Fire''-class bulk cruiser in the Ryloth system, thanks to Commander Syndulla. If the Alliance can secure more of these ships, the Quasar Fire could fill the role of escort carrier.|Anj Zavor, in a message to Mon Mothma|<ref name="Rebel Files" />}}
[[File:Zavor-Draven-Harinar-RO.png|thumb|left|300px|alt=Anj Zavor stands among other rebels behind Davits Draven in the Great Temple on Yavin 4.|Zavor served as part of Alliance High Command.]]
Anj Zavor was a [[human]] who [[Homeworld|hailed]] from [[Majoros]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> and served as a [[colonel]] in [[Rebel Fleet Command|Fleet Command]] for the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|navy]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="UVG" /> He<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> sent a message to [[Commander-in-Chief|Commander]] [[Mon Mothma]], head of the Alliance, informing her that the Rebellion had finished converting [[Mon Calamari]] [[city-ship]]s to war production facilities in the [[Telaris cometary cloud]]. The [[officer]] noted that the [[MC75 Star Cruiser]] ''[[Profundity]]'' would be the first [[cruiser]] to be combat-ready at the [[Telaris rebel stardocks|stardocks]] and, in an addendum, he mentioned the [[Phoenix Nest|''Quasar Fire''-class cruiser carrier]] that had been [[Mission to Ryloth (Phoenix Squadron)|acquired]] by [[Commander]] [[Hera Syndulla]] in the [[Ryloth system]]<ref name="Rebel Files" /> in [[3 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Zavor provided details on the [[Quasar Fire-class cruiser-carrier|carrier model]] and suggested that they could fill an escort carrier role if more could be acquired.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

Zavor later became liaison between the rebel forces of [[Massassi Group]], who were based at the rebel headquarters in the [[Great Temple]] of the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]], and [[Admiral]] [[Raddus]], [[Commanding officer|commander]] of the ''Profundity'' and the Alliance Fleet. Zavor kept a channel of communication open between Yavin 4 and the admiral, who was constantly mobile. Zavor was also a member of [[Alliance High Command]]<ref name="UVG" /> and was listed as Raddus's liaison in a list of the command members on a classified intelligence document titled Form #49021804-REB, which, along with Zavor's message to Mothma, was included in the collection of documents that became known as ''[[The Rebel Files]]''.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

===Prelude to Scarif===
[[File:ScarifMeeting-RO.png|thumb|right|300px|alt=Anj Zavor stands in a large crowd of rebels including Mon Mothma around a table in the Great Temple on Yavin 4.|Anj Zavor attended a meeting to discuss the Death Star plans on Scarif.]]
In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="RODate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'' to [[1 BBY]].</ref> Zavor was among the members of Alliance High Command who observed the questioning and recruitment of the criminal [[Jyn Erso]] into the Alliance in the Great Temple. Erso later returned to the temple with information from her [[Parent|father]], [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[scientist]] [[Galen Walton Erso|Galen Erso]], which revealed that the Galactic Empire was building a [[superweapon]] known as the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] that was capable of destroying [[planet]]s.<ref name="RO">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

However, Galen had created a flaw in the weapon that the rebels could exploit if they recovered the [[Death Star plans|plans]] for the [[battle station]] from the planet [[Scarif]]. A meeting was then held to discuss what should be done with the information, with Jyn and Raddus demanding that the Alliance attack Scarif. Zavor attended the meeting standing behind [[General]] [[Davits Draven]], but the plan of attack ultimately failed to gain unanimous backing from the Rebel Council. After the meeting disbanded, Jyn led an unauthorized [[Rogue One|squad]] of Alliance forces to Scarif in order to steal the plans.<ref name="RO" />

===Scarif and Yavin===
{{Quote|In other news, Col. Zavor has established contact with Ackbar and the remaining fleet elements. Expect a status report soon.|Jan Dodonna, in a message to Mon Mothma|<ref name="Rebel Files" />}}
When the rebels on Yavin 4 learned of the squad on Scarif, they scrambled their forces to provide support, with Raddus leading the [[fleet]] from the ''Profundity''.<ref name="RO" /> Zavor then carried out his liaison duties for Raddus during the ensuing [[Battle of Scarif]], in which the plans were successfully stolen, but Raddus and many others rebels were [[Death|killed]].<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> With Raddus gone and the battle over, Zavor managed to establish contact with Admiral [[Gial Ackbar]] and the remaining fleet elements, which General [[Jan Dodonna]] reported to Mothma. However, Ackbar reported that his forces were shorthanded, behind schedule, underequipped, and in no position to replace Raddus or bolster the rebel fleet.<ref name="Rebel Files" /> After the plans were eventually delivered to the Great Temple on Yavin 4, the [[Death Star]] itself traveled to the [[Yavin system]] in order to destroy the rebel headquarters there.<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref>

[[File:Rogues_Gallery.jpg|thumb|left|280px|alt=Anj Zavor stands behind Bob Hudsol at a medal ceremony for Luke Skywalker and Han Solo in the Great Temple on Yavin.|Anj Zavor attended a medal ceremony after the Battle of Yavin.]]
Zavor was then present for the [[Battle of Yavin]],<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> in which the Alliance successfully used the plans' information to destroy the Death Star.<ref name="ANH" /> The [[Local day|morning]] after the Alliance victory,<ref name="Morning">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref> an [[Royal Award Ceremony|award ceremony]] was held in the temple in which [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] presented [[Medal of Bravery|Medals of Bravery]] to [[Luke Skywalker]] and [[Han Solo]], [[pilot]]s who had played key roles in the battle. During the ceremony, Zavor stood upon the stage behind Organa alongside Dodonna and other members of Alliance High Command.<ref name="ANH" /> The rebels then evacuated all personnel from Yavin 4.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="RiseDate">{{RiseAndFallDate}}</ref> the [[historian]] [[Beaumont Kin]] included an image taken by the Great Temple's internal security of Zavor at the meeting where Erso revealed the flaw in the Death Star in<ref name="Rise">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> his<ref name="TROSVD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> [[book]] ''[[The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''.<ref name="Rise" />

==Personality and traits==
Anj Zavor had [[Color|light]] skin, gray [[hair]], and brown [[eye]]s.<ref name="Encyclopedia" />

==Equipment==
Prior to the Battle of Scarif,<ref name="RO" /> Zavor wore a brown [[Clothing|shirt]] with tan pants, a brown [[belt]], and a tan jacket that was part of traditional [[Alderaanian]] military livery.<ref name="UVG" /> He wore a [[rank insignia plaque]] with five red pips on his jacket.<ref name="RO" /> During the awards ceremony, Zavor wore a tan [[Hat|cap]], a white neckerchief, a green jacket, green pants, black shoes, and a black belt.<ref name="ANH" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|When populating the rebel command pages of the R1 Visual Guide, I looked at past named personnel across many sources, and thought this guy could work as Anj Zavor, a background Rebel named by Leland Chee in an Insider article (issue 133).|Pablo Hidalgo|<ref name="Pablo Hidalgo">{{Twitter|pabl0hidalgo|status/1729883026539389006|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=When populating the rebel command pages of the R1 Visual Guide, I looked at past named personnel across many sources, and thought this guy could work as Anj Zavor, a background Rebel named by Leland Chee in an Insider article (issue 133).|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/nUXNp}}</ref>}}
[[File:AnjZavor-ANH.jpg|thumb|right|250px|alt=A closeup of actor Henry Roberts as Anj Zavor in ''A New Hope''.|Anj Zavor was portrayed by Henry Roberts in ''A New Hope''.]]
Anj Zavor was portrayed by an uncredited [[Henry Roberts]]<ref name="ShowMaster">{{WebCite|url=https://www.showmasterssales.com/products/henry-roberts-10x8-signed-in-silver-image-a|text=Henry Roberts 10X8 Signed in Silver - Star Wars|work=[http://showmasterssales.com Showmasters Comic Con Official Autograph Shop]|archivedate=20210228175648}}</ref> in the [[1977]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="ANH" /> The medal ceremony scene was shot on Stage H at [[Shepperton Studios]] between [[May 13]] and [[May 18]], [[1976]].<ref name="MakingOf">''[[The Making of Star Wars]]''</ref> The character was then first identified in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity in the "[[Rogues Gallery (department)|Rogues Gallery]]" feature, written by [[Leland Chee]], of [[Star Wars Insider 133|133th issue]] of the ''[[Star Wars Insider]]'' magazine,<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|133|Rogues Gallery|Rogues Gallery: Celebrating a Rebel Victory!}}</ref> published on [[May 1]], [[2012]].<ref name="Titan">{{TitanMagazines|url=t/star-wars-insider/us/133|text=Star Wars Insider #133}}</ref>

Author [[Pablo Hidalgo]] decided<ref name="Pablo Hidalgo" /> that a character played by a separate actor in the [[2016]] [[canon]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|Anthology Series]] film, ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'',<ref name="RO" /> worked as a depiction of Zavor<ref name="Pablo Hidalgo" /> and identified him as such in the accompanying reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''. Although the book identifies Zavor as a colonel,<ref name="UVG" /> his [[Military rank|rank]] plaque in the film bears five pips,<ref name="RO" /> which the guide identifies as the insignia of a general.<ref name="UVG" />

